      "side": 1,
      "message": "The previous logic using `LoadTableFromTT()` validated that `offset` and `size` were within the bounds of `filesize` before attempting to allocate memory or read from the file. You should add a similar bounds check here to avoid potentially allocating a huge amount of memory for `names_data` if `loc-\u003esize` is maliciously crafted, and to prevent integer overflow.\n\nSomething like:\n```cpp\nif (loc-\u003eoffset \u003e filesize || loc-\u003esize \u003e filesize - loc-\u003eoffset) {\n  return;\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "3840e859ede8670370eafa220978f414cc5a39d2",
